            <ArticleTitle>[Strontium-89 diagnosis and therapy of bone metastases].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>658-62</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A clinical test of strontium-89 chloride effect was carried out in 150 patients with bone metastases and bone pain from different patterns of tumor. Different types of bone lesions were considered. Pain-relieving effect was reported in 77%, irrespective of lesion gravity. There was no response to strontium-89 chloride in 150 patients with bone metastases. It mostly occurred in cases of lysis. Strontium-89 chloride therapy contributed to partial bone tissue repair. It is indicated as a component of complex treatment for bone metastases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
